00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.470
- I've opened your sinks
and then the saddest part-

00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:58.303
- 'Cause I'm renovating.

00:00:58.303 --> 00:00:59.136
- You're renovating.
- Yes.

00:00:59.136 --> 00:01:01.180
- So there were, I opened four big boxes.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:02.723
So four sinks and I was like,

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.000
did I order sinks?

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:06.840
Like these aren't mine.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.480
I had to be like,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.151
was this one o'clock on a Unisom

00:01:11.151 --> 00:01:15.280
and did I order a bunch of sinks?

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.640
And then it was like, Kelly.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:17.660
I was like, oh, for God's sake.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:19.620
- I don't know why people have
a hard time with my address,

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.470
but whatever.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:22.340
But how are your kids doing?

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.470
- They're good.
- [Kelly] They're good.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:24.473
- They're great, yeah.

00:01:24.473 --> 00:01:26.490
- Yeah, they're giants.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.323
I don't understand what's happening.

00:01:27.323 --> 00:01:28.790
- I hear them playing in the backyard.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:29.623
- It's pickleball.

00:01:29.623 --> 00:01:30.494
It's pretty serious pickleball.

00:01:30.494 --> 00:01:31.327
- Yeah, we're big into pickleball now.

00:01:31.327 --> 00:01:32.610
- So I just got that

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.600
'cause somebody told me here
on set, I think it Wiess,

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.500
told me about pickleball
and I'd never heard of it.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:37.686
- [Melissa] Well it's-
- Do you play?

00:01:37.686 --> 00:01:38.941
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:01:38.941 --> 00:01:40.010
- Yes, intensely.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.340
- There's a stupid Sunday thing.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.987
We wear all whites just to be extra stupid

00:01:43.987 --> 00:01:45.562
and to look like ghosts.

00:01:45.562 --> 00:01:46.395
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:46.395 --> 00:01:48.780
I like it 'cause I grew up
playing tennis and I love it.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.240
But now I'm like-
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.010
- I'm gonna shatter all of it.

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:52.843
- [Ben] Yeah.

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:53.676
- Which I can't play tennis anymore.

00:01:53.676 --> 00:01:56.300
- When we first played,
Melissa got really competitive

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:58.217
and was just rifling balls at our kids.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.330
And I was like, "Mooch let's go easy."

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.253
She's like "No."

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:03.010
(Melissa laughs)
- Teach them, teach them.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.901
They're gonna have to win for real.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:05.320
- [Melissa] There's something
about a paddle, but then also,

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.150
if I see a ball, literally
in my head I'm like,

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:10.173
be nice, be nice, be
nice, be nice, be nice,

00:02:10.173 --> 00:02:12.530
be nice you son of a (beep).

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:16.378
And something takes over
from years of playing tennis.

00:02:16.378 --> 00:02:17.211
- Yeah.

00:02:17.211 --> 00:02:18.860
- And like I have hit
my kids and I'm like,

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.150
I'm a monster and I'm fine

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.650
until right when I'm about to swing,

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.037
then it's like, I'm gonna murder it.

00:02:26.037 --> 00:02:27.170
And I can't control myself.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.260
- [Kelly] I didn't know
that you played tennis.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.270
So I did not.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:32.290
And I got this house just
because of the location, really?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:34.320
And there happens to be a tennis court

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.153
in my backyard-

00:02:35.153 --> 00:02:35.986
- [Melissa] Have you played at all?

00:02:35.986 --> 00:02:36.819
- That we skate on.
- Yeah, yeah

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:39.670
- And we do a lot of other
things on it and ride bikes.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.750
But we don't play tennis, yeah.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.500
But now I wanna play tennis with you

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.182
'cause I want you to
get really competitive.

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:46.020
(Melissa and Kelly laugh)

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.853
- It's not pretty.

00:02:46.853 --> 00:02:47.830
It's really not pretty.

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:48.780
- And then I want you to watch

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.638
just two crazy women.

00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:50.910
- [Ben] I'll be like, no, no, no, no, no,

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:51.743
okay, fine.

00:02:51.743 --> 00:02:53.490
- You're like ow, ow, ow.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.420
- So wait, so Ben posted this photo

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:58.693
